    {
      "id": "p0103-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In Japanese, snakes make a \"shaaaa\" sound when they hiss, so Parsnik normally says shaaaa during battle. Parsnik's alternate hissing sound was localized as pyaaaa, which rhymes with shaaaa and refers to a legendary Japanese message board post involving a funny face shouting \"pyaaaa\" for no clear reason.",
        "raw": "In Japanese, snakes make a \"shaaaa\" sound when they hiss, so Parsnik normally\nsays shaaaa during battle. Parsnik's alternate hissing sound was localized as\npyaaaa, which rhymes with shaaaa and refers to a legendary Japanese message\nboard post involving a funny face shouting \"pyaaaa\" for no clear reason.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09561452,
          0.3023,
          0.70085445,
          0.37007143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09358017,
          0.30158571,
          0.70583861,
          0.37114286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日语中，蛇的嘶声是 shaaaa，Parsnik 战斗时也通常如此。另一声则译成 pyaaaa，与 shaaaa 押韵，还引用了日本论坛上的传奇帖子：一个滑稽表情莫名其妙地大喊“pyaaaa”。",
        "status": "draft",
